  "description": "YUYDED crystallizes in the monoclinic crystal system with space group C 2/c. Reported CIF formula moiety: C48 H50 Dy6 N20 O18 S8,6.5(C2 H3 N1),C1 H4 O1,2(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Dy1 (Dy) has 5 O neighbors; Dy2 (Dy) has 5 O neighbors; Dy3 (Dy) has 6 O neighbors; Dy1A (Dy) has 5 O neighbors; Dy2A (Dy) has 5 O neighbors; Dy3A (Dy) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 6 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.505-3.540 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 92.18-100.78°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Dy6L2(μ3-OH)4(μ2-OH)2(SCN)8(H2O)4]·6CH3CN·2CH3OH·H2O. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 μ3-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 μ2-OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
